questions.statement:
Consider the following reaction scheme and choose the correct option(s) for the major products $\mathbf{Q}$, $\mathbf{R}$ and $\mathbf{S}$.

$$
\begin{array}{c}
\text{Styrene} \xrightarrow[\text{(ii) NaOH, H}_2\text{O}_2, \text{H}_2\text{O}]{\text{(i) B}_2\text{H}_6} \mathbf{P} \xrightarrow[\begin{array}{c} \text{(ii) Cl}_2, \text{Red phosphorus} \\ \text{(iii) H}_2\text{O} \end{array}]{\text{(i) CrO}_3, \text{H}_2\text{SO}_4} \mathbf{Q} \\
\mathbf{P} \xrightarrow[\begin{array}{c} \text{(ii) NaCN} \\ \text{(iii) H}_3\text{O}^+, \Delta \end{array}]{\text{(i) SOCl}_2} \mathbf{R} \xrightarrow{\text{conc. H}_2\text{SO}_4} \mathbf{S}
\end{array}
$$
